=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# ssh screen-legacy-main ---------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: SSH Login. web-01.example.net runs Debian 13 (OpenSSH$
# 10.0p2). origin/main's hardn.conf (PermitRootLogin no,$
# AuthenticationMethods publickey, AuthorizedKeysFile$
# .ssh/authorized_keys). 50-cloud-init.conf, read first, sets$
# PasswordAuthentication yes, but AuthenticationMethods$
# publickey keeps passwords out.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [ ] SSH Port             Not Configured default (22)$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Disallowed by hardn.conf$
   -  Password Login       Off by AuthenticationMethods$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
  [ ] Old Settings         hardn.conf$
   -  Logged in as         george, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Allow root key-only  Root logs in by key alone$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
   4) Move old settings    Into 00-hardn.conf$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-4 or q]:$
$
$

